- name: clay
  type: table
  desc: Functions and constants for building Clay UI layouts.
  members:
  - name: initialize
    type: function
    desc: Creates a Clay layout surface whose retained GUI nodes are parented to the supplied GUI node. max_element_count determines the Clay arena and per-layout metadata capacity for this surface and defaults to 8192. Destroy and recreate the surface to change it.
    parameters:
    - name: root_node
      type: userdata
      desc: GUI node used as the layout bounds and parent for generated nodes.
    - name: max_element_count
      type: number
      desc: Optional maximum number of Clay elements for this surface. Defaults to 8192.
      optional: true
    returns:
    - type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface handle.

  - name: destroy
    type: function
    desc: Deletes generated GUI nodes and releases a Clay surface. Call from the GUI script final function.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.

  - name: begin_layout
    type: function
    desc: Begins a new Clay layout. The layout dimensions are synchronized automatically from the initialized root GUI node's effective on-screen bounds, including window adjustment.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.

  - name: element
    type: function
    desc: Retains a root element declaration. Supports id, layout, floating, transition, background_color, overlay_color, corner_radius, border, clip, image, layer, slice9, children, and on_hover. layer accepts a GUI layer name or hash and applies only to this element's render commands; layers are not inherited. A transition requires duration and a property bitmask assembled from TRANSITION_PROPERTY_* constants; Clay interpolates between the element's previous and current declared state using its native ease-out handler. Enter, exit, and rounded-corner transitions are not currently exposed. Transitioned elements should use stable IDs. floating accepts offset, expand, parent_id, z_index, attach_points, pointer_capture_mode, attach_to, and clip_to. ATTACH_TO_ELEMENT_WITH_ID requires parent_id to be a global ID declared earlier in the tree. Set clip.scroll to true to use Clay's managed scroll offset for a horizontally and/or vertically clipped element. on_hover(element, pointer) runs during end_layout while that native element is open, so it supports local IDs and may mutate visual or layout fields for the current layout. pointer contains x, y, and state. An image can be a GUI texture name or hash, or a table with texture and optional atlas animation names or hashes. corner_radius is rendered on background rectangles and ordinary images by the Clay GUI material. If an image also has a nonzero slice9, slice9 is preserved and shader rounding is disabled because Defold's nine independently interpolated patches do not provide one continuous shape coordinate. slice9 must be a vmath.vector4 and is forwarded independently to the generated Defold GUI node.
    parameters:
    - name: element
      type: table
      desc: Element declaration. The id may be nil, string, hash, or a value returned by a Clay id helper. on_hover must be a function when supplied.

  - name: end_layout
    type: function
    desc: Completes the layout and reconciles Clay render commands with retained GUI nodes.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    - name: dt
      type: number
      desc: Optional frame delta time in seconds. Defaults to zero.
      optional: true

  - name: text
    type: function
    desc: Creates a text-node declaration for use in an element's children array.
    parameters:
    - name: text
      type: string
      desc: Text to display.
    - name: config
      type: table
      desc: Text configuration. font_id is required and accepts a GUI font name or hash. font_size defaults to the size authored in that font resource. Optional fields are text_color, letter_spacing, line_height, and layer. layer accepts a GUI layer name or hash and is not inherited.
    returns:
    - type: table
      desc: A Clay text-node declaration.

  - name: id
    type: function
    desc: Creates a global Clay string id.
    parameters:
    - name: value
      type: string
      desc: Id string.
    returns:
    - type: userdata
      desc: Clay id descriptor.

  - name: idi
    type: function
    desc: Creates an indexed global Clay id.
    parameters:
    - name: value
      type: string
      desc: Base id string.
    - name: index
      type: number
      desc: Numeric id offset.
    returns:
    - type: userdata
      desc: Clay id descriptor.

  - name: id_local
    type: function
    desc: Creates a Clay id local to the currently open parent element.
    parameters:
    - name: value
      type: string
      desc: Id string.
    returns:
    - type: userdata
      desc: Clay id descriptor.

  - name: idi_local
    type: function
    desc: Creates an indexed Clay id local to the currently open parent element.
    parameters:
    - name: value
      type: string
      desc: Base id string.
    - name: index
      type: number
      desc: Numeric id offset.
    returns:
    - type: userdata
      desc: Clay id descriptor.

  - name: sizing_fixed
    type: function
    desc: Creates a fixed-size Clay sizing axis.
    parameters:
    - name: size
      type: number
      desc: Fixed size in pixels.
    returns:
    - type: userdata
      desc: Clay sizing descriptor.

  - name: sizing_grow
    type: function
    desc: Creates a growing Clay sizing axis with optional bounds.
    parameters:
    - name: min
      type: number
      desc: Optional minimum size. Defaults to zero.
      optional: true
    - name: max
      type: number
      desc: Optional maximum size. Defaults to unbounded.
      optional: true
    returns:
    - type: userdata
      desc: Clay sizing descriptor.

  - name: sizing_fit
    type: function
    desc: Creates a fit-content Clay sizing axis with optional bounds.
    parameters:
    - name: min
      type: number
      desc: Optional minimum size. Defaults to zero.
      optional: true
    - name: max
      type: number
      desc: Optional maximum size. Defaults to unbounded.
      optional: true
    returns:
    - type: userdata
      desc: Clay sizing descriptor.

  - name: sizing_percent
    type: function
    desc: Creates a Clay sizing axis relative to its parent.
    parameters:
    - name: percent
      type: number
      desc: Parent-relative size factor.
    returns:
    - type: userdata
      desc: Clay sizing descriptor.

  - name: set_pointer_state
    type: function
    desc: Hit-tests the previous completed layout and updates Clay's pointer state. Call before begin_layout. The screen position is transformed into the initialized root GUI node's top-left layout space.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    - name: x
      type: number
      desc: Defold screen-space pointer x coordinate, normally action.screen_x.
    - name: y
      type: number
      desc: Defold screen-space pointer y coordinate, normally action.screen_y.
    - name: pressed
      type: boolean
      desc: Whether the pointer is currently pressed.

  - name: get_pointer_state
    type: function
    desc: Returns Clay's current pointer coordinates and interaction state.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    returns:
    - type: table
      desc: Table with x, y, and state fields.

  - name: hovered
    type: function
    desc: Returns whether the pointer overlaps a globally identified element in the previous completed layout. This is an alias for pointer_over.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    - name: id
      type: any
      desc: String, Defold hash, or global Clay id helper value.
    returns:
    - type: boolean
      desc: True when the pointer overlaps the element.

  - name: pointer_over
    type: function
    desc: Returns whether the pointer overlaps a globally identified element in the previous completed layout.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    - name: id
      type: any
      desc: String, Defold hash, or global Clay id helper value.
    returns:
    - type: boolean
      desc: True when the pointer overlaps the element.

  - name: get_pointer_over_ids
    type: function
    desc: Returns the numeric Clay ids under the current pointer, ordered by Clay's hit-test traversal.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    returns:
    - type: table
      desc: Array of numeric Clay ids.

  - name: update_scroll_containers
    type: function
    desc: Applies wheel deltas, pointer dragging, and momentum to Clay scroll containers from the previous layout. Call after set_pointer_state and before begin_layout every frame.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    - name: enable_drag_scrolling
      type: boolean
      desc: Enables pointer-drag scrolling.
    - name: scroll_x
      type: number
      desc: Horizontal scroll delta.
    - name: scroll_y
      type: number
      desc: Vertical scroll delta.
    - name: dt
      type: number
      desc: Frame delta time in seconds.

  - name: get_scroll_container_data
    type: function
    desc: Returns the retained scroll state for a globally identified clipped element, or nil when it has not completed a layout as a scroll container.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    - name: id
      type: any
      desc: String, Defold hash, or global Clay id helper value.
    returns:
    - type: [table, nil]
      desc: Table with position, container_size, content_size, horizontal, and vertical fields, or nil.

  - name: set_scroll_position
    type: function
    desc: Sets the retained offset of a globally identified scroll container. Values normally range from negative overflow to zero.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    - name: id
      type: any
      desc: String, Defold hash, or global Clay id helper value.
    - name: x
      type: number
      desc: Horizontal scroll offset.
    - name: y
      type: number
      desc: Vertical scroll offset.
    returns:
    - type: boolean
      desc: True when the scroll container was found.

  - name: set_culling_enabled
    type: function
    desc: Enables or disables Clay offscreen element culling.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    - name: enabled
      type: boolean
      desc: Whether culling is enabled.

  - name: set_debug_mode_enabled
    type: function
    desc: Enables or disables Clay's built-in debug layout for one surface. Enabling requires a GUI font named Default or default, which is reserved as Clay font id zero.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    - name: enabled
      type: boolean
      desc: Whether the Clay debug layout is enabled.

  - name: is_debug_mode_enabled
    type: function
    desc: Returns whether Clay's built-in debug layout is enabled for a surface.
    parameters:
    - name: surface
      type: userdata
      desc: Clay surface returned by initialize.
    returns:
    - type: boolean
      desc: Whether the debug layout is enabled.

  - name: LEFT_TO_RIGHT
    type: constant
    desc: Horizontal child layout direction.

  - name: TOP_TO_BOTTOM
    type: constant
    desc: Vertical child layout direction.

  - name: ALIGN_X_LEFT
    type: constant
    desc: Align children to the left.

  - name: ALIGN_X_RIGHT
    type: constant
    desc: Align children to the right.

  - name: ALIGN_X_CENTER
    type: constant
    desc: Center children horizontally.

  - name: ALIGN_Y_TOP
    type: constant
    desc: Align children to the top.

  - name: ALIGN_Y_BOTTOM
    type: constant
    desc: Align children to the bottom.

  - name: ALIGN_Y_CENTER
    type: constant
    desc: Center children vertically.

  - name: ATTACH_POINT_LEFT_TOP
    type: constant
    desc: Floating attachment point at the left top.

  - name: ATTACH_POINT_LEFT_CENTER
    type: constant
    desc: Floating attachment point at the left center.

  - name: ATTACH_POINT_LEFT_BOTTOM
    type: constant
    desc: Floating attachment point at the left bottom.

  - name: ATTACH_POINT_CENTER_TOP
    type: constant
    desc: Floating attachment point at the center top.

  - name: ATTACH_POINT_CENTER_CENTER
    type: constant
    desc: Floating attachment point at the center.

  - name: ATTACH_POINT_CENTER_BOTTOM
    type: constant
    desc: Floating attachment point at the center bottom.

  - name: ATTACH_POINT_RIGHT_TOP
    type: constant
    desc: Floating attachment point at the right top.

  - name: ATTACH_POINT_RIGHT_CENTER
    type: constant
    desc: Floating attachment point at the right center.

  - name: ATTACH_POINT_RIGHT_BOTTOM
    type: constant
    desc: Floating attachment point at the right bottom.

  - name: POINTER_CAPTURE_MODE_CAPTURE
    type: constant
    desc: Floating element captures pointer interaction from elements behind it.

  - name: POINTER_CAPTURE_MODE_PASSTHROUGH
    type: constant
    desc: Pointer interaction passes through the floating element.

  - name: ATTACH_TO_NONE
    type: constant
    desc: Disables floating behavior.

  - name: ATTACH_TO_PARENT
    type: constant
    desc: Attaches a floating element to its declarative parent.

  - name: ATTACH_TO_ELEMENT_WITH_ID
    type: constant
    desc: Attaches a floating element to the global ID in floating.parent_id.

  - name: ATTACH_TO_ROOT
    type: constant
    desc: Attaches a floating element to the Clay layout root.

  - name: CLIP_TO_NONE
    type: constant
    desc: Floating element does not inherit its attached element's clipping.

  - name: CLIP_TO_ATTACHED_PARENT
    type: constant
    desc: Floating element inherits its attached element's clipping.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_NONE
    type: constant
    desc: No transition properties.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_X
    type: constant
    desc: Transition the element's horizontal position.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_Y
    type: constant
    desc: Transition the element's vertical position.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_POSITION
    type: constant
    desc: Transition both position axes.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_WIDTH
    type: constant
    desc: Transition the element width.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_HEIGHT
    type: constant
    desc: Transition the element height.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_DIMENSIONS
    type: constant
    desc: Transition width and height.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_BOUNDING_BOX
    type: constant
    desc: Transition position and dimensions.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_BACKGROUND_COLOR
    type: constant
    desc: Transition the background color.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_OVERLAY_COLOR
    type: constant
    desc: Transition the overlay color.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_BORDER_COLOR
    type: constant
    desc: Transition the border color.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_BORDER_WIDTH
    type: constant
    desc: Transition the border widths.

  - name: TRANSITION_PROPERTY_BORDER
    type: constant
    desc: Transition border color and widths.

  - name: TRANSITION_DISABLE_INTERACTIONS_WHILE_TRANSITIONING_POSITION
    type: constant
    desc: Disable pointer interactions while position is transitioning.

  - name: TRANSITION_ALLOW_INTERACTIONS_WHILE_TRANSITIONING_POSITION
    type: constant
    desc: Allow pointer interactions while position is transitioning.

  - name: POINTER_PRESSED_THIS_FRAME
    type: constant
    desc: Pointer transitioned to pressed during the latest pointer update.

  - name: POINTER_PRESSED
    type: constant
    desc: Pointer remains pressed.

  - name: POINTER_RELEASED_THIS_FRAME
    type: constant
    desc: Pointer transitioned to released during the latest pointer update.

  - name: POINTER_RELEASED
    type: constant
    desc: Pointer remains released.
